<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=radio">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Communication and computing</p><h1 class="enc-title">Radio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1895">1895</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as wireless telegraphy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Radio is communication by electromagnetic waves sent through the air; after Heinrich Hertz showed in experiments published between 1886 and 1888 that such waves could be transmitted, the Italian inventor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guglielmo-marconi">Guglielmo Marconi</a> was field testing a wireless system by August 1895 and applied for a British patent in 1896. It was first used for 'wireless telegraphy' in Morse code, and on 12 December 1901 Marconi sent a message across the Atlantic. Audio transmission followed in the early 1900s, and by 1919–1920 regular entertainment broadcasts were heard in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/radio.jpg" alt="Radio" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marconi_and_his_wireless_apparatus_1897.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1895</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Guglielmo Marconi</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Heinrich Hertz had sent radio waves through the air in 1886–1888, and Alexander Popov and Jagadish Chandra Bose demonstrated receivers in 1895.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">Electrical telegraph<span>1816</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/electromagnetic-induction">Electromagnetic induction<span>1831</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/television">Television<span>1909</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/mobile-phone">Mobile phone<span>1973</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=radio">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
